# The free demo's configuration, Vue edition: who ships it, and where they live.
#
# The same two keys as `apps/web/free-react/.env.example`, under Vite's prefix instead of Next's,
# because Vite cannot read `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` and neither can read the other's. The pair is deliberately
# not shared: this is the one part of the two editions that has to differ, and the fallbacks in code
# match so an unconfigured demo of either reads identically.
#
# Everything else is absent and honestly so: every page renders from fixtures in its own file, so
# there is no API to point at, no database, no auth and nothing secret. Its own URL is not
# configuration either, since it is built into the marketing site's `public/` and served at
# `/preview/free-vue`, a path that is correct in every environment.
#
# The footer is the exception. A buyer shipping this template is not Viliha, and saying so should be
# two keys rather than a component edit, which is the difference between a template and a fork. The
# name is rendered verbatim: casing is part of how a company writes its own name.
VITE_SITE_NAME=
VITE_SITE_URL=
